<h1>Changelog</h1>
<p>Notable changes since version 42.0.0, read the complete <a href="https://jdbc.postgresql.org/documentation/changelog.html">History of Changes</a>.</p>
<p>The format is based on <a href="http://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/">Keep a Changelog</a>.</p>
<h2>[Unreleased]</h2>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>fix: <code>PGStream.skip</code> no longer loops forever when the connection ends while the driver is discarding bytes, and no longer mistakes a stream that skips nothing for one that has ended. <code>InputStream.skip</code> may return zero with more data still coming, which a stream supplied through the <code>socketFactory</code> property is free to do; the driver now reads a byte in that case and treats only <code>-1</code> as the end [PR <a href="https://redirect.github.com/pgjdbc/pgjdbc/issues/4358">#4358</a>](<a href="https://redirect.github.com/pgjdbc/pgjdbc/pull/4358">pgjdbc/pgjdbc#4358</a>)</li>
<li>fix: <code>LargeObjectManager</code> operations now work inside an active XA transaction. Since 42.7.13 an XA branch keeps the caller's <code>autoCommit=true</code>, and the guard rejected large objects as if the connection were idle. It now checks the server transaction state (<code>getTransactionState()</code>) instead of <code>autoCommit</code>, so a genuine auto-commit connection with no open transaction is still refused [Issue <a href="https://redirect.github.com/pgjdbc/pgjdb"}]

